Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix:=20resolve=20all=208=20dashboard=20bugs=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20charts,=20scenarios,=20EDA,=20polling?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug 1 — Chart data wrong order:
  Initial history load from API returns newest-first (ORDER BY timestamp DESC).
  Added .slice().reverse() on initial load in Dashboard, HealthAnalytics,
  and EnvironmentalIntelligence so charts render chronologically.

Bug 2 — Scenario readings all same timestamp:
  For-loop called datetime.now() synchronously, giving 10 identical timestamps.
  Staggered timestamps 2s apart in backend/api/routes/scenarios.py.

Bug 3 — GET /scenarios/active missing:
  Added module-level _active_scenario tracker and GET /scenarios/active route
  to scenarios.py so the UI can query the current scenario.

Bug 4 — Redundant polling loops:
  7 intervals fired on WS disconnect (per-page useEffects).
  Removed disconnect-polling useEffect from Dashboard, HealthAnalytics,
  EnvironmentalIntelligence. App.jsx always-on 800ms polling handles fallback.

Bug 5 — EDA always 0/empty:
  Added eda ranges to all 4 scenarios in simulator/scenarios.py and added
  eda field generation in simulator/data_generator.py.

Bug 7 — api.risks.history duplicate:
  api.risks.history pointed to same endpoint as api.risks.recent.
  Removed duplicate; callers updated to use api.risks.recent directly.

Bug 8 — AIRiskAnalysis loses history on remount:
  useState([]) reset on every navigation. Now persists via store.riskHistory
  and store.riskData in dataStore singleton; skips API fetch if cache warm.

